   <urn:stardog:demos:movies:rating> "8.2"^^xsd:float ;
   <urn:stardog:demos:movies:storyline> "In 1922, the country boy Harold says goodbye to his mother and his girlfriend Mildred in the train station and leaves Great Bend expecting to be successful in the big city. Harold promises to Mildred to get married with her as soon as he \"make good\". Harold shares a room with his friend \"Limpy\" Bill and he finally gets a job as salesman in the De Vore Department Store. However, he pawns Bill's phonograph, buys a lavaliere and writes to Mildred telling that he is a manager of De Vore. One day, Harold sees an old friend from Great Bend that is a policeman and when he meets his friend Bill, he asks Bill to push the policeman over him and make him fall down. However Bill pushes the wrong policeman that chases him, but he escapes climbing up a building. Out of the blue, Mildred is convinced by her mother to visit Harold without previous notice and he pretends to be the manager of De Vore. When Harold overhears the general manager telling that he would give one thousand dollars to to anyone..." ;
   <https://schema.org/inLanguage> "English" .
<http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0015324> a <https://schema.org/Movie> ;
   rdfs:label "Sherlock Jr." ;
   <https://schema.org/description> "A film projectionist longs to be a detective, and puts his meagre skills to work when he is framed by a rival for stealing his girlfriend's father's pocketwatch." ;
   <https://schema.org/actor> <http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0000036> , <http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0175068> , <http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0444172> , <http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0570230> ;
